<title>BELGIUM: W.Europe car registrations down 5.2 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>W.Europe car registrations down 5.2 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are provisional West European new car registrations and market share figures for November released on Thursday by the European Automobile Manufacturers Association (ACEA).</p>
<p> Brand		   Nov 96    pct change  mkt share vs Nov 95</p>
<p>							    (pct)	 (pct)</p>
<p> All brands	    903,300    -5.2pct</p>
<p> Volkswagen	    162,000    -0.5	     17.9	 17.1</p>
<p> GM			110,491    -7.7	     12.2	 12.6</p>
<p> PSA		     100,942   -13.2	     11.2	 12.2</p>
<p> Ford		     98,921    -6.9	     11.0	 11.2</p>
<p> Fiat		    106,500    -9.5	     11.8	 12.4</p>
<p> Japanese		 93,713     2.8	     10.4	  9.6</p>
<p> Renault		  87,786    -7.5		9.7	 10.0</p>
<p> BMW			65,707     1.8		7.3	  6.8</p>
<p> Mercedes		 34,600     2.7		3.8	  3.5</p>
<p> Korean		   18,338     7.6		2.0	  1.8</p>
<p> Volvo		    18,784    10.8		2.1	  1.8</p>
<p>(Volkswagen includes Audi, Seat, Skoda. GM includes Opel/Vauxhall, U.S. imports  aUSGIM/A, Saab, IBC/ISUZU. PSA includes Peugeot, Citroen. Fiat includes Lancia, Alfa Romeo, Innocenti, Ferrari, Maserati. Ford includes U.S. imports, Jaguar. BMW includes Rover. Japanese includes Nissan, Toyota, Mazda, Honda, Mitsubishi, other.)</p>
